atem:
  line: tally counts named things from the command line in an append-only ledger, so concurrent adds are never lost
    and any add can be undone.
  focus: A three-command tool, add, show and undo, over a ledger file that is only ever appended to.
  push: Count small things without a spreadsheet, and trust the counts, because nothing is ever overwritten.
  pull: The safety of concurrent adds rests on the operating system appending one short line at a time, which the
    code assumes and does not check.
