- id: N:decision/append-only-log
  type: decision
  name: An append-only log, not a totals file
  summary: In 0.2 the ledger became an append-only log of entries instead of one JSON file of totals rewritten on
    every add.
  stance: observed
  chose: one JSON object per line, appended, with totals folded from the whole log when needed
  over:
  - option: one JSON file of totals, rewritten on every add (0.1)
    because: two adds at once could lose one, and nothing could be undone
  because: Appending never loses an earlier count and keeps every step, so undo can walk back.
  by: R:maker/meadow
  changed-in:
  - R:change/append-only-log
  span:
    file: CHANGES.md
    lines: 5-6
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - CHANGES.md#L5-L6
    confidence: 0.9
    state: pending
  made:
    move: ground
    run: 2026-11-18-1200-a901
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: code
- id: N:decision/undo-by-opposite
  type: decision
  name: Undo appends the opposite
  summary: An undo appends the opposite of the entry it cancels and names that entry's line, instead of removing
    anything.
  stance: deduced
  chose: append an entry with the opposite delta and undoes set to the cancelled line's number
  over:
  - option: remove the last line
    because: it would rewrite the ledger, which the log forbids
  because: It keeps the ledger append-only, and naming the cancelled line lets a second undo skip it and walk further
    back.
  changed-in:
  - R:change/undo-added
  span:
    file: tally/ledger.py
    lines: 73-84
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tally/ledger.py#L73-L84
    confidence: 0.8
    state: pending
  made:
    move: ground
    run: 2026-11-18-1200-a901
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: code
