- id: C:behaviour/add
  type: behaviour
  name: An add appends and reports
  summary: tally add checks the name and the number, appends one line to the ledger, then reads the whole ledger
    back and prints the name's new total.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/command.add
  - C:interface/tally.ledger.add
  when: tally add NAME [N]
  does: 'Strips NAME; refuses an empty name, a name with whitespace, or N of 0; creates the ledger''s folder if
    needed; appends {"at", "delta", "name"}; prints NAME: TOTAL.'
  edges:
  - given: tally add pages -2
    then: a negative N is read as the number, not an option; pages goes down by 2
  - given: a ledger that does not exist yet
    then: it is created, with its parent folders
  errors:
  - when: tally add "two words"
    message: 'tally: a name is one word, with no spaces'
    exit: 1
  - when: tally add tea 0
    message: 'tally: adding 0 changes nothing'
    exit: 1
  - when: tally add with no name
    message: argparse's usage and its 'the following arguments are required' line
    exit: 2
  span:
    file: tally/ledger.py
    lines: 61-70
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tally/ledger.py#L52-L70
    - tally/cli.py#L36-L39
    confidence: 0.9
    state: pending
  made:
    move: ground
    run: 2026-11-18-1200-a901
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: code
- id: C:behaviour/undo
  type: behaviour
  name: Undo walks back
  summary: tally undo looks back from the newest line for an add that is neither an undo nor already undone, and
    appends its opposite naming its line.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/command.undo
  - C:interface/tally.ledger.undo
  when: tally undo
  does: 'Reads every entry; collects the line numbers that undo entries name; from the last entry to the first,
    takes the first that has no undoes and is not named; appends {name, delta: -delta, undoes: its line}; prints
    "undid D on NAME; NAME: TOTAL", D being the cancelled entry''s delta with its sign (undid +1, undid -2).'
  edges:
  - given: undo after undo
    then: the second cancels the add before the first's; an undo is never itself undone
  - given: every add already undone, or an empty ledger
    then: prints "nothing to undo", writes nothing, exit 0
  span:
    file: tally/ledger.py
    lines: 73-84
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tally/ledger.py#L73-L84
    - tally/cli.py#L48-L54
    confidence: 0.9
    state: pending
  made:
    move: ground
    run: 2026-11-18-1200-a901
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: code
