- id: C:behaviour/show
  type: behaviour
  name: Show draws bars
  summary: tally show prints one row per name, the name padded, the total right-aligned and a bar of '#' scaled
    so the largest positive total gets 30.
  stance: observed
  of:
  - C:interface/command.show
  - C:interface/tally.render.rows
  when: tally show [--all] [--json]
  does: Names in alphabetical order; a total of 0 is left out unless --all; each row is NAME padded to the longest
    name, two spaces, TOTAL right-aligned to the widest total, two spaces, the bar, with trailing space removed;
    a bar is round(total * 30 / largest positive total) characters, at least one for any positive total; a negative
    total has no bar. --json prints the same totals (0 left out unless --all) as one JSON object with sorted keys.
  edges:
  - given: 'totals {a: 10, bb: 1, c: 0}'
    then:
    - 'a   10  ##############################'
    - 'bb   1  ###'
  - given: 'totals {a: -2}'
    then:
    - a  -2
  - given: no rows to show
    then: 'prints empty_message: "nothing tallied yet (or every total is 0; try --all)", or "nothing tallied yet"
      with --all'
  intended:
    pending: is hiding totals of 0 by default intended, or a choice users would change?
  span:
    file: tally/render.py
    lines: 8-25
  provenance:
    mode: derived
    sources:
    - tally/render.py#L8-L29
    - tally/cli.py#L40-L47
    confidence: 0.9
    state: pending
  made:
    move: ground
    run: 2026-11-18-1200-a901
    step: 1
    node: '1'
    engine: code
