- id: C:reliance/whole-numbers-unbounded
  type: reliance
  name: whole numbers without limit
  summary: Whole numbers have no fixed width.
  stance: observed
  'on': language
  gives: Whole numbers have no fixed width. Adding, subtracting and multiplying them never overflows and never loses
    a digit, however large they grow.
  example: 18446744073709551615 plus 1 is 18446744073709551616, exactly; a total past two to the sixty-third is
    kept.
  stated:
  - in: python
    version: 3.13.18
    at: builtins/stdtypes.html#numeric-types-int-float-complex
    digest: 736b53f803b0
