    with status 2. The messages are fixed phrases: "the following arguments are required: X", "unrecognized arguments:
    A B", "argument X: invalid choice: ''V'' (choose from a, b)" (the choices unquoted, as 3.13.11 was recorded;
    earlier releases quoted them), "argument X: invalid int value: ''V''", "argument X: ignored explicit argument
    ''V''", "ambiguous option: --x could match --xa, --xb". Values are shown in their quoted form. A sub-command''s
    errors name it ("tool add") and print its own usage line; words a sub-command does not take are reported by
    the top level.'
